</pre> <p><code>HadronFileReader.h</code> and the example macros live in js-contrib, in <code>contribs/PyJetscape/example/analysis_root/</code>. We copy the ones we need next to our macros: from your js-contrib (a checkout or the installed tree), or else from GitHub. Copies, because ACLiC writes its compiled library next to the macro, and an installed tree may be read-only.</p> In [7]: Copied! <pre>import shutil
import urllib.request

ANALYSIS_ROOT = ("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jhputschke/js-contrib/main/"
                 "contribs/PyJetscape/example/analysis_root/")

def analysis_root_file(name):
    """Copy analysis_root/&lt;name&gt; into OUT: from the local js-contrib, else from GitHub."""
    try:
        from jetscape import paths
        src = Path(paths.examples_dir()) / "analysis_root" / name
    except Exception:
        src = None
    if src is not None and src.is_file():
        shutil.copy(src, OUT / name)
        return "js-contrib"
    urllib.request.urlretrieve(ANALYSIS_ROOT + name, OUT / name)
    return "GitHub"

for name in ["HadronFileReader.h", "read_hadrons.C", "hadron_distributions.C"]:
    print(f"{name:24s} from", analysis_root_file(name))
